      <div type="clause" n="40">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Ine">Ine</ref> 40</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="40" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="106" ed="#liebermann"/>LXXXIIII. Ceorles worðig<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#Ine_40.lnote.oe.11-2"/> sceal beon wintres ⁊ sumeres betyned; gif he bið untyneð, ⁊ recð his neahgebures<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#Ine_40.lnote.oe.12"/> ceap in on his agen geat, nah he æt þam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#Ine_40.lnote.oe.13"/> ceape nan wuht<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#Ine_40.lnote.oe.14"/>: adrife hine ut ⁊ ðolie<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#Ine_40.lnote.oe.15"/> æfwerdlan.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="40" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="106" ed="#liebermann"/>LXXXIIII. Ciorles wurðig<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Ine_40.lnote.oe.6-2"/> sceal<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Ine_40.lnote.oe.7-2"/> beon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Ine_40.lnote.oe.8"/> wyntres<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_40.lnote.oe.3"/> ⁊ sumeres betyned; gif he biþ untyned, ⁊ receþ<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Ine_40.lnote.oe.9"/> his neahgebures ceap on his agen geat in, nah he æt þam ceape<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_40.lnote.oe.4"/> nan wuht<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#Ine_40.lnote.oe.10"/>: adrife hit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#Ine_40.lnote.oe.11"/> ut ⁊ þolie (þone<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#Ine_40.lnote.oe.10"/>) æfwyrdlan.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_40.lnote.oe.3"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="40" corresp="#wit-b-no-prol"><pb n="106" ed="#liebermann"/>Be ceorles worðige. Ceorles worði sceal beon wintres ⁊ sumeres betyned; gyf he bið untyned, ⁊ recð his nehhebures ceap in on his agen geat, nah he æt ðam ceape nan wiht: adrife hine ut ⁊ ðolie ðone æfwyrlan.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="40" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="107" ed="#liebermann"/>Ceorles ƿeorðig<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Ine_40.lnote.oe.5"/> (id est rustici curtillum) debet esse clausum estate simul et<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Ine_40.lnote.oe.6"/> hieme. Si disclausum sit, et introeat alicuius uicini sui captale<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Ine_40.lnote.oe.7"/> per suum apertum, nichil inde recipiat, sed educat et patiatur dampnum suum.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="48" ed="#attenborough"/>[Be ceorles worðige.] Ceorles worðig sceal beon wintres ⁊ sumeres betyned. Gif he bið untyned<ptr type="editorNote" n="13" target="#Ine_40.attnote.fn.13"/>, ⁊ recð his neahgebures ceap in on his agen geat, nah he æt þam ceape nan wuht<ptr type="editorNote" n="14" target="#Ine_40.attnote.fn.14"/>: adrife hine<ptr type="editorNote" n="15" target="#Ine_40.attnote.fn.15"/> ut ⁊ ðolie [þone]<ptr type="editorNote" n="16" target="#Ine_40.attnote.fn.16"/> æfwerdlan<ptr type="editorNote" n="17" target="#Ine_40.attnote.fn.17"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="41" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="406" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>{LXXXIIII} Ceorles worðig sceal beon wintres ⁊ sumeres betyned. Gif he bið untyneð, ⁊ recð his neahgebures ceap in on his agen geat, nah he æt þam ceape nanwuht: adrife hine ut ⁊ ðolie æfwerdlan.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="107" ed="#liebermann"/>Des Bauern Hofstelle<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_40.lnote.de.1"/> soll Winters und Sommers umzäunt sein; wenn sie nicht umzäunt ist, und seines Nachbarn Vieh dringt ein in seine eigene [die vom Bauern gelassene] Öffnung, so erhält er nichts<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_40.lnote.de.2"/> von diesem Vieh: (sondern<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_40.lnote.de.3"/>) er treibe es<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_40.lnote.de.4"/> aus und leide den<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Ine_40.lnote.de.5"/> Schaden.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Ine_40.lnote.de.6"/></ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">The peasant’s homestead is to be fenced winter and summer; if it is not fenced, and his neighbour’s livestock gets in through his own opening [the one left by the peasant], he gets nothing from that livestock: (but) let him drive it out and suffer the damage.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="49" ed="#attenborough"/>A commoner's premises shall be fenced both winter and summer. If they are not enclosed, and a beast belonging to his neighbour strays in through the opening he himself has left, he shall have no claim on that beast, [but] he shall drive it out and suffer the damage.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="404" ed="#whitelock"/>A <hi rend="italic">ceorl’s</hi> homestead must be fenced winter and summer. If it is not fenced, and his neighbour’s cattle get in through his own gap, he has no right to anything from that cattle; he is to drive it out and suffer the damage.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="407" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>A <hi rend="italic">ceorl</hi>’s pasturage shall be fenced winter and summer. If it is not fenced, and his neighbor’s livestock strays in through his own opening, he has no claim on the livestock: let him drive it out and suffer the damage [that the livestock did].</ab>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_40.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">107</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-rdic <hi rend="italic">Or;</hi> -ðit <hi rend="italic">K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-rdic Or; -ðit K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_40.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">107</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ab <hi rend="italic">K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ab K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_40.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">107</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">capit. <hi rend="italic">stets T;</hi> oues uel caprae <hi rend="italic">am Rande Co</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">capit. always T; oues uel caprae in the margin Co</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_40.lnote.oe.6-2" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">106</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">u <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">u on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_40.lnote.oe.7-2" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">106</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">geänd. aus</hi> sceol</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">altered from sceol</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_40.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">106</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">e <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">e on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_40.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">106</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">y <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">y on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_40.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">106</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">eþ <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">eþ on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_40.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">106</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">übergeschr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">written above</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_40.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">106</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_40.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">106</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">t <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">t on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_40.lnote.oe.11-2" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">106</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">weorþig <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">weorþig Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_40.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">106</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">nehg. <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">nehg. Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_40.lnote.oe.13" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">106</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ðæm <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ðæm Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_40.lnote.oe.14" n="14" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">106</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">wiht, ac <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">wiht, ac Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_40.lnote.oe.15" n="15" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">106</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ðolige ðone æfwyrdlan <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ðolige ðone æfwyrdlan Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_40.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">75</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Gehege 2; Bauer 13d. Noch jetzt heisst in Niedersachsen <hi rend="italic">word</hi> die Wohn- und Wirtschaftsstätte samt Platz für Gemüsebau, Garten, Stall für Arbeits- und Jungvieh; Hanssen in <hi rend="italic">Gött. Gel. Anz.</hi> 1870, 1327. Diese Hofstättenumzäunung ist auch in Deutschland Pflicht; Nasse <hi rend="italic">Feldgemeinschaft</hi> 12; für Wales belegt sie Price für den Garten</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Gehege 2; Bauer 13d. Even now in Lower Saxony <hi rend="italic">word</hi> denotes the dwelling and farm site, together with space for growing vegetables, the garden, and the stable for working cattle and young stock; Hanssen in <hi rend="italic">Gött. Gel. Anz.</hi> 1870, 1327. This fencing of the homestead is a duty in Germany too; Nasse <hi rend="italic">Feldgemeinschaft</hi> 12; for Wales Price attests it for the garden</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_40.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">75</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Pfändung (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 6a) daran ist verboten</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Distraint (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 6a) of it is forbidden</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_40.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">75</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Sinngemässer Zusatz, vielleicht 11. Jhs., in lq</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">An addition in keeping with the sense, perhaps of the 11th cent., in lq</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_40.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">75</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">H ändert grammat. Genus ins Neutrum</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">H changes the grammatical gender to neuter</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_40.lnote.de.5" n="5" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">75</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">H cor. B führen modernisierend Artikel ein</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">H cor. and B, modernising, introduce the article</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_40.lnote.de.6" n="6" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">75</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Den das fremde Vieh seinem Hof und Garten antat</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">That which other people's cattle did to his homestead and garden</seg></note>
